{"agent":"fx-hand-record","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new check is inserted into the shared record path and refuses command-gate `passed` records for which `evidence.ran_by` is empty. However, the only place setting `evidence.ran_by` is `ddflow ci run` (`ddflow/api/cirun.py`); the `ddflow gate run` path is unchanged and still leaves `ran_by` at its default `\"\"`. A legitimate `ddflow gate run <id> <command_gate>` that executes the command successfully will produce evidence with `command` and `exit_code=0` but no `ran_by`, so `HR.hand_record` will classify it as a hand record and refuse it. This regresses the primary way a command gate is passed. The manifest confirms `gate run` is exercised by `tests/test_gate_run_after_merge.py` (modified in this change) but no corresponding `ran_by` assignment was added for that path.","digest":"e1e2e19efd65e16d","location":"ddflow/api/gates.py:1198-1204 (HR.hand_record call)","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/gates.py:1198-1204 (HR.hand_record call)"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The refusal is gated on `agent_why` being truthy, so a never-run command gate is still accepted when no reason text is supplied. The bug's own repro, `ddflow gate record <id> unit_tests --outcome passed --command 'pytest -q' --exit-code 0`, has no `--reason`, so this line returns `\"\"` immediately, `hand_record` returns `(\"\", {})`, and the unit_tests gate is still recorded as passed with no run. The change therefore does not close Bed643a611b for the exact input it claims to fix.","digest":"8b0cc09a578fac7f","location":"ddflow/services/gates/handrecord.py:20","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/gates/handrecord.py:20"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The hand-record setup in `test_gate_record_keeps_the_output_file_it_digests` clears only `CLAUDECODE`, but the companion autouse fixture in `tests/test_gate_econ_tests.py` explicitly clears both `CLAUDECODE` and `DDFLOW_AGENT` because the suite itself may run under an agent harness. Under an environment with `DDFLOW_AGENT` set, this test still looks like an agent to the new `handrecord.py` refusal path, so the `gate record --command` call it makes is refused instead of accepted as a person’s hand record, causing the test to fail in exactly the supported agent-harness environment the change is meant to handle.","digest":"4f34efed8b7574d3","location":"tests/test_gate_output_evidence.py:82","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_gate_output_evidence.py:82"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`_setup` configures `unit_tests` with `command = {sys.executable} -c \"print('1 passed')\"`, while `HAND` supplies `--command \"pytest -q\"`. The regression test therefore does not reproduce Bed643a611b as stated, where the recorded `--command` belongs to the configured, never-run gate. A faulty fix that rejects only when the supplied `--command` differs from the configured command would satisfy `test_an_agent_cannot_hand_record_a_never_run_command_gate_passed`, while still accepting the original bug when the recorded command matches the configured command. The test should arrange the configured command and the recorded command to be the same (or otherwise exercise a matching command) to ensure the refusal is truly caused by the no-run rule.","digest":"22a239f0e50a7dd0","location":"tests/test_gate_record_by_hand_command.py:28-38","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_gate_record_by_hand_command.py:28-38"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"This test calls `_setup(repo, monkeypatch)` with no claim argument, so it never calls `ddflow claim T1`. Since the sibling test explicitly uses `_setup(repo, monkeypatch, \"--no-worktree\")` to create a no-tree state, a normal claim is what would produce the tree that this first test asserts: `assert ev[\"tree_sha\"] and \"tree_sha\" not in ev.get(\"unmeasured\", [])`. Without that claim, the fixed code records `tree_sha` as unmeasured/absent, so the test fails on the intended behavior.","digest":"46a2bafae834e6c9","location":"tests/test_gate_record_measured_fields.py:test_a_hand_record_names_the_host_of_its_output_file_and_what_it_did_not_measure","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_gate_record_measured_fields.py:test_a_hand_record_names_the_host_of_its_output_file_and_what_it_did_not_measure"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16178,"diff_sha":"03247e7b271f1fb897d07c2c5caeec02c122ef045547e366f06a808702bcc25a","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":453.6,"family":"deepseek","findings":5,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"ca18b40159bcfe02","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bed643a611b.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261022T104826Z-5cff8805.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"f103a64f70622d3984e2f7986ca570dcdf065fe8","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/cirun.py":"100644 b813d56c126c1bc45ec21775569875e02871d541","ddflow/api/gates.py":"100644 08a3da4d2a9696f2d2da91261f775e7d8c9fe2c1","ddflow/services/gates/__init__.py":"100644 69381d6d034dc4f6358c382002eb730d02fcbf0f","ddflow/services/gates/handrecord.py":"100644 45263551045d31fbd3ac227d09324f2f0808cd44","ddflow/services/report_gates.py":"100644 4f96dd3068e8e16bd61b1a30d0962f405523af4d","tests/test_gate_econ_tests.py":"100644 ebded893f176f25e816bb29d680340a49c26fbac","tests/test_gate_output_evidence.py":"100644 dcedc4be5aa0d800f0f3974be68e5413ec5dbf62","tests/test_gate_record_by_hand_command.py":"100644 7a8dbb0605ebd2dc5aa643669077865ef8f41cc1","tests/test_gate_record_measured_fields.py":"100644 ce50861cb54876c74d842f90b5a08190f7bef797","tests/test_gate_run_after_merge.py":"100644 5d390e176dd82a9f6ac7bcce9b26adf24c130933"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":[